# EcoDrug Project Structure

This is a full-stack ecological mobile application called "ЭкоДруг" (EcoDrug).

## Project Overview
- **Purpose**: Universal digital solution for promoting environmentally responsible behavior
- **Target Audience**: Citizens, eco-activists, students, volunteers, NGOs, eco-companies
- **Main Features**: Eco news, events calendar, recycling point map, educational materials, gamification

## Project Structure

### Backend (`/backend`) - Node.js + Express + MongoDB
- `/models` - MongoDB schemas (User, Profile, Course, News, Event, RecyclingPoint, Achievement, etc.)
- `/routes` - API endpoint definitions
- `/controllers` - Business logic for each module
- `/middleware` - Authentication (JWT), validation, error handling
- `/config` - Database connection, environment configuration
- `/utils` - Helper functions
- `/tests/unit` - Unit tests
- `/tests/integration` - Integration tests

### Frontend (`/frontend`) - Flutter Web (later mobile)
- `/lib/models` - Dart data models
- `/lib/services` - API service layer (HTTP calls, token management)
- `/lib/screens` - UI screens (Login, Register, Profile, News, Events, Map, etc.)
- `/lib/widgets` - Reusable UI components
- `/lib/utils` - Helper functions and constants

## Key Technologies
- **Backend**: Node.js, Express, MongoDB, JWT, bcrypt, CORS
- **Frontend**: Flutter Web (Dart), Provider (state management), shared_preferences
- **Database**: MongoDB (local dev, MongoDB Atlas for production)
- **Authentication**: JWT tokens with bcrypt password hashing

## Core Modules (11 total)
1. Authorization - registration, login, JWT security
2. Profile - user data, achievements, roles (user/organization)
3. Education - articles, courses, tests, videos
4. News - feed, moderation, categories
5. Events - calendar, event cards, registration
6. Map - recycling points with filtering
7. Gamification - points, achievements, levels, contribution visualization
8. Notifications - reminders and push notifications
9. Support - donations
10. Organizations - verified NGO and company profiles
11. Admin Panel - content moderation, organization verification

## Important Guidelines
- Always use JWT for authentication
- Hash passwords with bcrypt before storing
- Use CORS for frontend-backend communication
- Implement role-based access control (user/organization/admin)
- Follow modular architecture - keep concerns separated
- All user-generated content requires moderation
